he structural rules, not full equivalence)\n- [ ] Detects a single swapped pair (2 wires) when one pair of gate outputs is exchanged → test: swap two structurally-distinguishable wires (e.g. a `z` output XOR with an internal AND), expect exactly those 2 wires returned\n- [ ] Detects 4 independent swapped pairs (8 wires total) in a 45-bit adder → test: programmatically swap 4 structurally-distinguishable pairs across different bit positions, expect exactly the 8 wires returned, sorted\n- [ ] Returned array is sorted lexicographically → test: assert array equals `[...].sort()`\n- [ ] Runs in well under 5s for a 45-bit (~220 gate) circuit with 4 swapped pairs → test: assert wall-clock time bound (e.g. < 2000ms)\n- [ ] Correctly identifies the final carry-out z-bit (highest index) as exempt from the \"z output must be XOR\" rule → test: verify an unmodified final-OR-to-z gate is not flagged\n\n## Build/lint\n\n- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds with no TypeScript errors\n- [ ] `npm run lint` succeeds with no lint errors\n- [ ] `npm test` passes all tests\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
